{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfcgPmAz4EQnsabNvCMjx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe functional/response reshaping is largely idiomatic — `formatIdentity` building the `OwnerIdentityDto` lives correctly in `OwnerMapper`, `apiVersion` as a MapStruct `constant`, pre-deriving `ownerSegment` at the call site mirrors the existing `membershipLevel` pattern (respecting the deliberate audit→mapper decoupling), the `schemaVersion`/`SCHEMA_VERSION` constant on the event record, and the removal of the now-dead `memberIdRegion` helper when `locality` stopped reading the region from the member id. Those are all in the right units.\n\nOne structural issue:\n\n**Duplicated `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant across two units.** The same private constant, with the same name, same value, and near-identical explanatory comments, is now declared independently in both `model/Owner.java` (for `identityKey`) and `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (for `generateMemberId` and `householdIdFor`). This is one business concept — the identity version tag — expressed as two sources of truth. A move to V3 would require remembering to change both, and nothing links them. Since `ClinicServiceImpl` already depends on `Owner` (model), the natural fix is a single shared constant (e.g. a `public static final String IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG` on `Owner`, or a small dedicated identity-version holder) that both the entity's `getIdentityKey()` and the service's member-id/household-id derivation reference, so the three identifiers provably share one tag definition rather than three coincidentally-equal literals.\n\nEverything else reads as a coherent, additive version-2 change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16700,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ep